	doi = {10.5281/zenodo.13251118},
	abstract = {CoralBlox is a coral growth and mortality model. It allows the simulation of distinct coral functional groups indirectly competing for a limited space over time. The model does not consider disturbances such as deaths cause by cyclone, COTS or heat stress. It also does not have a direct mechanism to contemplate human interference such as coral seeding or cloud brighten. Despite that, one can leverage CoralBlox to include coral growth and mortality to a broader model.

 

